der than anybody else  but we seem to be treated differently  are they scared of us why is that for  Marcia and thousands of others this has  been a summer of protests my sons are  stopped and searched  they've been stopped and searched since  they were 10 years old my children get  Rachel  looks and stares because of the dad's  dark and I've got two films with blonde  hair and they automatically are judging  in what's going on their blood the  summers protests were already well  underway when news broke of another  death this time it was Mo's a Muhammad  just 18 years old police say they were  called to reports of a man acting  erratically at a Liverpool shopping  center footage shows him surrounded by  police and security guards he would soon  be dead  hay was already so much anger at black  deaths following police contact and then  the here in Liverpool with a Muhammad  died the grief is really raw I've come  to the opening of the inquest to speak  to his family as they begin their search  for answers they already have concerns  about how the IPCC's investigation is  progressing for some at least maybe get  one answer but it's like they're sitting  back and taking the time it's not  acceptable than 18 you know especially  being our family and our loved one  snatched away off the streets and no  justice and nothing's done about it and  people want i pc that want to react as  fast as they acted on the day these 18  years of age of his life spoon taking  away he's never gonna see a day he's  never gonna get a chance to advocate  he's never going to see the child again  they've now joined the growing number of  families at the heart of the black lives  matter movement  Kingsley Burrell died after calling the  police  fearing he was being targeted by violent  youths he was detained under the Mental  Health Act for four days an inquest  found prolonged restraint and a failure  to provide medical care contributed to  his death Kings was vulnerable and when  they arrived